=== CupRoundDriver (Kick.cs / Scene.cs partials) ===
public bool LocalIsFreed { get; }   // NEW: Local/Host = LocalBody.Freed && Active && !Parked; Client = derived from the mirrored state (scorer in a scored window; in Free Kicks anyone on the side that just scored (Line.Last.Side == Setup.LocalSide); the winning side in the win beat). CupHud.LocalFreed returns true on it (the seam edit), so a freed free-kick teammate gets the wheel + legend.
Behaviour changes (same signatures): Live entry calls SetKickClock(0f); PlaceForKick recomputes the free-kick marks (AssignFreeKickMarks) and never walks a taker in for Free Kicks; ParkAllAtMarks uses the idle scatter while Idle and the FIRST KICK's layout (twin visibility per the kick's rule) from the Intro on, then RefreshLocalBody(); BeginWalkBack in Free Kicks stands the taker down (Reset) and calls Choreo.OnMissDeject, TickWalkBack ends at CupTuning.FreeKickMissBeat; OpenScoredWindow in Free Kicks frees every active, visible human body on the scorer's side (not this kick's keeper) and CamHold()s a freed local teammate; TickFreedBodies ticks a freed KeeperController body that is not this kick's keeper (unlocked, HoldLine off); TickLive: `approaching` (c.z - BallRadius < GoalCenter.z && vel.z > LiveApproachSpeed && speed > LiveApproachSpeed) suppresses the RestHold and MaxLiveTime verdicts, LiveHardCap is unconditional, the goal test stays latch OR swept crossing OR BallFullyInGoal.
